    60	
    61	**First exchange.** She let him come. That was the whole of it, and it took twelve seconds and taught him more than the next thirty: he moved off the crown toward her at an angle that opened the road's northern shoulder behind him, and she did not close the shoulder, and did not step, and did not declare, and the shoulder shut anyway — a new point blooming at the culvert's mouth, twelve feet behind his left heel, laid there while he was still committing to the step that made it worth laying. Her lattice was not an attack. It was *subtraction*: exits priced and then removed, one at a time, at the rate he generated them. He arrived at fifteen feet from her with the western half of the cut no longer available and understood that he had bought the distance with the only thing he had that she wanted, which was ground.
    62	
