     7	The cascade had come on before dawn, real, on the constraint's own clock — the eighth acquisition's bill presenting mid-recovery the way the log had learned to expect and the body never quite did — and Cael managed it with the discipline three years had built: recovery days banked in advance, the circle warned the night before, nothing evaluable scheduled, the room cleared of everything that could be dropped, water and bread within reach of the bed, the door left unlatched so that nobody would have to break it.
     8	
     9	It came anyway, and it came strange, because the Anchor-adjacent component pulled like nothing before it.
