    32	
    33	The second, at the end, when the framework closed and the room went back to being a room and Cael lay there working out whether he could stand: "My father's forge had a floor that dropped a thumb's width in the north corner. Thirty years he never fixed it. He said a man who knows exactly where his floor is wrong is safer than a man on a flat one he's never measured." He stood up and took the chair back where it came from. "You've measured. That's the part that's yours."
