    63	The first went to a man who kept the mould room at the south mill. Eleven years ago Seln had filed one true sentence about him instead of a sentence that would have been more useful to somebody else, and the man had never known which office to thank, but he had known whom. The letter asked one thing. *Was the registry mould mended this year, and if so, when, and was a run made off it after?* It did not say who wanted to know. It did not have to.
    64	
    65	The second went west.
