    72	
    73	At the foot of the road the two coats stood under the eaves of the chandler's warehouse, as close to the wall as they could get. They watched him come down. He let them. He had passed them perhaps two hundred times, and they had written him down perhaps two hundred times as the wing's assistant, with the post. He walked past them at the pace of a man who wanted to be dry and said, "Wet one," and the nearer one said, "It is," and that was all.
    74	
