   159	The road took the skin off it. He felt it go from the wrist to the elbow, a long hot scrape, as if somebody had drawn a rasp up the inside of his forearm. He came to rest on his side at the bottom of the camber, a few yards short of the channel, with his face in the dust and his right side one solid ache.
   160	
