   162	
   163	Ten counts. It always came after a lane, since Norhold, and it came now: everything he owned answering a beat late. The right thing, slow. *Bill, not flag*, Lira had written in her palm on the honest floor. He tried to get his hands under him and they got there a beat after he asked. He tried to turn his head to find her and his neck turned a beat after that.
   164	
   165	One.
   166	
   167	She laid a point.
   168	
   169	He felt it go in, near his left shoulder, against the chalk.
   170	
