   191	He felt every bar of it. They were not the fourteen; the fourteen were still out in the cut where they had always been, at the mouths and in the banks and on the milestone. These were new. They were close. They stood round him at the height of his knees and his shoulders and his head, a ring of points two feet off on every side, and above him, and on the chalk under him. He counted them twice. Nineteen.
