   198	
   199	He could feel the lines now, faintly, through the read. They ran from the point on his coat out to the nineteen round him, and from the nineteen out to the fourteen in the cut, and from all of them, all of them, back to her. She stood on her flat patch of crown fifteen feet away with every line in the cut running into her two loose hands like the reins of a team.
   200	
