   231	The near horse threw up its head and stamped, and stood on all four legs again as a horse should. The coachman's hands came down into his lap with the reins in them.
   232	
   233	Karis looked at her own hand in the air above nothing, and took it back.
   234	
   235	She felt it in her hands.
   236	
   237	He saw that. He was still on his knees and he saw her feel her whole morning go out through her fingers, fourteen points laid before light and every one she had laid since, all of them at once. She did not stagger. She did not make a sound. Her two loose hands closed, slowly, as if somebody had pulled a rope out of them faster than she could hold it.
   238	
   239	She lifted two fingers of her left hand.
   240	
   241	The team broke off in four heartbeats.
   242	
