   250	
   251	Then she turned and went up the north bank on the rope, hand over hand, without the half beat, and over the top into the grass, and was gone.
   252	
   253	He knelt in the road. The wind came along the cut from the west and blew the chalk dust off the crown in a long white skirl and carried it away east over the culvert.
   254	
   255	Brom was walking toward him down the channel, with his left arm hanging.
