editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/EVENT-LIST.md:17:| 87 | Third-day | **The eleventh of Sowing. Eighteen.** The annex; paper face-down; Ephram (from grievances, early); the tally; Seln's room line; Hesk's satchel and note; Lira's three bouts aloud; inventory eight; *Still open…*; the sill; Seln at the door at the tenth bell |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/EVENT-LIST.md:24:1. **Seln, day 77, before the first bell** (cutaway). Way in: the records hall dark except Bracken's counter lamp; Seln waits for Bracken to finish winding the counter clock. One question: where did the mark sit when you held it to the light? Bracken had laid his ivory rule on the sheet at the lodge window, because he lays a rule on everything; a sixteenth of an inch low against the south mill's registry stock. Seln says thank you and nothing else. Bracken does not ask why. Seln knows what a sixteenth means: a mould re-laid after a wire went; everything off it is a second run. (His own sample-sheets of registry stock in the back of a manual — the habit of a man who copies things.)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/EVENT-LIST.md:25:2. **Seln, same day.** The favours, counted: four owed to him in fifteen years, never spent. Two letters in the service hand at the copying table, each a single question: to the man who keeps the south mill's mould room (the run); west to a correspondent in the registry's western stores (the lots drawn off that run). The price of a favour is that it tells somebody you wanted to know. He walks down the bluff road on the rest day with a clerk's satchel; the coats see a clerk with letters; the drop behind a chandler's counter near the bridge; the bag that goes faster than the post. On the way back up he counts the coats and lets them count him.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/EVENT-LIST.md:31:1. **Seln, day 80–81** (cutaway). The mould-room answer on day 80 (in the man's own spelling): the registry mould re-laid this year; the mark a sixteenth low ever since; the second run. Day 81, the post-room sort (he still does it for the porter's shoulder), the service bag's envelope with the western answer, four lines: the second run's lots in the stores ledger, thirteen, each against an office; a fourteenth drawn above the ruled lines, and in the office column a mark where a word should be. He reads it twice and burns it in the sort-room stove, which is what the four lines were written to expect.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/EVENT-LIST.md:32:2. **Seln, the four grades.** He names them in the order the woman who taught them named them, in a room over a chandler's on a quay, his first year: the record (paper in a file); the instrument (a proceeding, in daylight); the knock (paper from an office nobody can place, at the door — it measures the door); the hand (no paper, no face, a road where no house stands). The fourth grade does not knock. A fourteenth lot is what the third grade looks like from the inside of a ledger. The fourth comes next.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/EVENT-LIST.md:78:2. **The annex, evening.** Karis's long table with every paper turned face-down, squared; the assistant brings up a cake from the kitchen and goes; Brom's spirit kettle; Lira on the window seat with the strapped foot on a stool; Karis's hand unwrapped today, the fingers a shade paler.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/EVENT-LIST.md:79:3. **Ephram.** He shuts grievances early for the first time in two years and comes; at the table he sees the face-down stacks, reads that they are face-down, and turns his chair to the window with his back to them, deliberately, without a word. His tally: ninety-one entries since the qualifying year, and a gap this week; he isn't asking about any of them; he wanted Cael to know somebody has been paying attention. Who sings: Brom, low, a Velmere harvest song all the way through, nobody joining; Ephram laughs at the last verse.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:20:- **Seln's window** (~5k): the paper traced (the watermark's sixteenth of an inch; the fourteenth lot with a mark where a word should be); two favors spent; the four grades of pressure, named in order; **the catechism, said once, and watching it lose** — quietly, the largest event of his adult life; the case carried across campus; **"You're sure." / "No. That's how you'll know it's true."**; the annex chosen; the floor-schedule cipher (five arrivals, not six); a null report filed in the old pattern — **not** "the last of its kind" (calendar: he keeps filing until the year's close).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:25:- **Eighteen**: the postponement by floor schedule; the cascade — **fixity**, forty courteous proposals an hour; **the doorway fixed for twelve seconds, uncommanded**; the idle state found by naming; Storm resettles twice; Brom's rota and the forge-floor line ("You've measured. That's the part that's yours."); Karis's curve, *for now*. The birthday: paper face-down; Ephram's tally; Seln's "It is a good room. I have been in a great many."; **Hesk's satchel and note**; Lira's three bouts said aloud. Inventory: eight. *Still open. Still real. Patience.*
