## Verdict

**Fail: 136 genuine tracked passages.** The zero-unprotected 8-word result does not describe the
source distance of this movement. Outside the protected text, the manuscript repeatedly retains a
source sentence's substantive beats in the source order, most often by replacing nouns and verbs,
adding local business, or cutting one long source sentence into several shorter ones. Chapter 14
and the hearing sequence in Chapter 20 are the heaviest concentrations; Chapter 19 is the most
continuously tracked chapter.

Counting unit: one continuous manuscript passage following one source sentence, or one tightly
unified source sentence-cluster, counts as one passage. When one source sentence becomes several
manuscript sentences, it is one **split** passage. I did not count exact Tier A/B or packet lines,
including the denial, folder tab, Daeva statement and letter, Hesk letter, Seln's protected lines,
the day-after line, the final coach lines, or other protected wording. I also did not count the new
wing-three bout, the honest-floor practice, or Seln's dramatized service-side circuit merely because
